As the internet cafe prepares to shut down, I see this as the perfect opportunity to showcase my skills and knowledge in software development. In this final project, I will guide you through the process of building a real-time chat application using WebSockets and Node.js. This project will demonstrate my understanding of web development, networking, and software architecture.

**Project Overview**

Our chat application will allow users to connect to a server and engage in real-time conversations with other users. The application will be built using Node.js, Express.js, and Socket.IO. We will use WebSockets to establish a bi-directional communication channel between the client and server.

**Step 1: Setting up the Project Structure**

Create a new directory for our project and initialize a new Node.js project using `npm init`. Install the required dependencies:

```bash
npm install express socket.io
```

Create a new file called `server.js` and add the following code to set up the Express.js server:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const server = require('http').createServer(app);
const io = require('socket.io')(server);

app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.sendFile(__dirname + '/index.html');
});

server.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server listening on port 3000');
});
```

**Step 2: Creating the Client-Side Code**

Create a new file called `index.html` and add the following code to set up the client-side code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Real-Time Chat Application</title>
  <script src="/socket.io/socket.io.js"></script>
  <script>
    const socket = io();

    // Send message to server
    function sendMessage() {
      const message = document.getElementById('message').value;
      socket.emit('message', message);
    }

    // Receive message from server
    socket.on('message', (message) => {
      const chatLog = document.getElementById('chat-log');
      chatLog.innerHTML += `<p>${message}</p>`;
    });
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Real-Time Chat Application</h1>
  <input id="message" type="text" />
  <button onclick="sendMessage()">Send</button>
  <div id="chat-log"></div>
</body>
</html
